# Why: Jason is fine with writing a few tests at once, as long as every one runs red before the code that passes them.
# Why: Stub new names before writing tests, so red means a failing assertion; tests requested for existing code go red by breaking the code briefly.
# Why: Point at mutate-check for breaking code briefly, so agents don't hand-roll backup/mutate/restore
# Why: Pick test seams yourself; ask only when the seam is a design fork.
